  "behavior": [
    "TimeLineView exposes layer, frame and span snapshots and directly sets the frame type. A valid unoccupied frame returns EMPTY. A stable layer ID follows its layer during reorder.",
    "MessageList projects nine typed columns to a native record array for bulk replacement. The snapshot preserves auxiliary fields and owns its text across widget mutation or close. Existing node attachments are governed by native whole-list replacement.",
    "C user pointer storage remains native. Language exports only data and sets no arbitrary user pointer.",
    "In 1000 warmed layer/frame/span rounds, the language makes 3000 balanced XRT allocations for nonempty text snapshots. The C counterpart uses borrowed text and makes zero allocations. Frame snapshots carry only scalars.",
    "In 1000 warmed reads of one full auxiliary message, the language makes 6000 balanced XRT allocations for six text fields. The C counterpart uses borrowed text and makes zero allocations.",
    "The tests inject early write failures after preparing the input columns and fail each text allocation prefix of the span and message snapshots. The last result and live heap are preserved. CPU timings and real-GPU rendering are outside this gate."
  ],
